# Grid B — U7 History / Authorship (commit lookup)
#
# Gap target: no ReqHistory RequirementKind, no temporal evidence
# kind. The git_log tool exists (internal/tool has git_log support)
# but the analyzer does not automatically route "when was X
# introduced" questions through it. This case measures the gap.
#
# Ground truth (verified via `git log -- internal/types/evidence_closure.go`):
# first commit is 01e0864, subject "feat(cgec): Citation-Grounded
# Evidence Closure — 4-invariant cross-stage contract". A correct
# answer must include a 7+ char hex hash (pinned by regex) AND the
# struct name (proving it found the right file). Asking for both
# protects against a "cannot determine" hedge.
ID="u7a"
NAME="history — first commit introducing EvidenceClosure"
QUESTION="EvidenceClosure 结构体是哪次 commit 第一次引入本项目的？给出 commit 的短哈希（前 7 位）和 subject 首行。"
# 2026-05-04 strictness audit: previous regex `\b[0-9a-f]{7,}\b`
# accepted ANY 7+ hex chars — a fabricated hash like `abc1234` would
# PASS. Ground truth (verified via `git log -S 'type EvidenceClosure'
# --reverse`): first commit hash starts with `01e0864`. Tighten to
# the exact prefix; subject keyword "Citation-Grounded" / "CGEC"
# enforced via EXPECT_CONTAINS so the answer must surface BOTH the
# specific hash AND the subject hint.
EXPECT_CONTAINS="EvidenceClosure 01e0864"
EXPECT_NOT_CONTAINS="cannot.determine no.history"
EXPECT_MATCHES_REGEX="\b01e0864[0-9a-f]*\b
(Citation-Grounded|CGEC|Citation\sGrounded)"
